  "base": "s1399",
  "failed_start_fallback": "s1399",
  "changes": {
    "conversations and cache": "one-bank shared inactive image budget up to 8 GiB (native production: 7 GiB shared, 6 GiB session cache, 16 entries); checkpoints for conversations shorter than 8,192 tokens and for a prefix shared by several conversations; a displaced conversation's image is reclaimed before a new one is refused; right-sized wide arenas",
    "prefill": "12 wide encoder widths instead of 5 (a chunk plan fitted to the prompt), a partially filled last wide chunk, the encoder checkpoint taken inside the chunk, the first token sampled before the tail of an append completes, and tokenization that reuses the cached ids of an unchanged prefix of a long message",
    "decode": "paced L2 prefetch hints for the expert weights, later routing statistics, a native expert front end, direct QKV projection reads, table rows read with O_DIRECT instead of through the page cache, a three-threshold draft ladder, and the drafter's vocabulary head in 4 bits over a script subset with pooled rows (drafts are verified against the unchanged target, so the sampled distribution does not depend on the drafter)",
    "several conversations at once": "batched decode: up to four conversations share one verification step, each in a serving region of 262,144 positions. A conversation shares only if its prompt plus its whole token limit (max_tokens; 262,144 when the request gives none) fits a region and it carries no image; every other conversation takes turns through paused images, and waits while regions are occupied. A paused or cached conversation restores into whichever drafter holds the first region, a resumed request keeps the checkpoints of the conversation it displaces, and a conversation in its first run yields after 16 tokens to one that has not started",
    "option, off by default": "CANADA_SCRATCH_HEAD4_RESCORE (the model's own output head read from a 4-bit copy with exact rescoring of the likely tokens): it changes the sampled distribution slightly by design and is in no default profile"
  },
  "unchanged": [
    "weights",
    "the target model's output head and sampler",
    "memory floor (8 GiB)",
    "2350 MHz clock policy",
    "portable profile"
